- How would you adjust thresholds if observed latency creeps above SLO during canary?
- What governance cadences would you enforce to keep all teams aligned over 8 weeks?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests ability to design governance for cross-team experimentation, balancing speed with reliability and data integrity.

## Key Concepts
- KPI ownership and charter
- Preflight power analysis and data-quality gates
- Guardrails: latency, error rate, quotas
- Feature flags, canary and cohort rollouts
- Artifacts: experiment charter, data map, rollback plan

## Code Example
```javascript
function shouldRollout(experiment, metrics) {
  const {power, mde, dataQuality} = metrics;
  if (!experiment.flagsEnabled) return false;
  if (power < experiment.requiredPower) return false;
  if (!dataQuality.ok) return false;
  if (metrics.latency > experiment.maxLatency) return false;
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would thresholds vary by product area?
- How would you measure guardrail impact on velocity and reliability?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to translate onboarding into concrete artifacts, rituals, and measurable outcomes for a distributed setting.

## Key Concepts
- Onboarding playbooks that scale across time zones
- Clear artifacts and acceptance criteria
- Lightweight rituals that sustain momentum
- Quantifiable ramp metrics and experiments

## Code Example
```javascript
function rampScore({timeToFirstCommit, issuesClosed, prMergeTime}) {
  const t = timeToFirstCommit <= 7 ? 1 : 0;
  const i = issuesClosed >= 5 ? 1 : 0;
  const p = prMergeTime <= 48 ? 1 : 0;
  return t + i + p;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you automate onboarding checklists and artifact generation?
- How would you adapt artifacts for contractors vs. full-time engineers?
